{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186162570 :knowledge-point/_questions [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186161967 :knowledge-point/id #uuid "908b96db-9463-50b5-89a3-056072c930ba" :knowledge-point/title "Using Row Operations to Create a Column of Zeros in a 3x3 Matrix" :topic/_knowledge-points [{:db/id #edb/ref 17592186050527 :topic/title "Creating Rows or Columns Containing Zeros Using Gaussian Elimination"}]}] :question/answer-fields [{:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "b1a477f1-10fc-50a1-981c-aae4b3c5dea0" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} - 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160713} {:answer/id #uuid "c0333c66-4f35-5f3c-9968-610aa5423fcf" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 3R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} - 2R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160714} {:answer/id #uuid "f2355978-048f-57b5-8eee-c677498630a1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} + 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160715} {:answer/id #uuid "175e8e59-45a0-515a-829f-30c1a15ea357" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} - 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} + 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160716} {:answer/id #uuid "1ea804c1-eba2-5894-a0db-ce41e6af71d1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "$R_{1}:=R_{1} + 2R_{2}$ and $R_{3}:=R_{3} - 3R_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160717}] :answer-field/id #uuid "8c3e10ff-3c11-531e-9e12-9a991205d1f5" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186160712} {:answer-field/choices [{:answer/id #uuid "f91cfd00-78b8-5e81-b3da-fb66e4a255b1" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404525} {:answer/id #uuid "ba816428-2269-5d70-a23d-de4d9459d350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404526} {:answer/id #uuid "6b221426-9041-561c-a939-a652454c20be" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+3{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-2{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404527} {:answer/id #uuid "7377369a-9c28-53fe-95a8-20a033d61460" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}+3{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404528} {:answer/id #uuid "4d223b12-1545-5649-89b4-f8afd0248272" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}-2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404529}] :answer-field/correct {:answer/id #uuid "ba816428-2269-5d70-a23d-de4d9459d350" :answer/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045499 :db/ident :answer.type/text} :answer/value "${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}$" :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404526} :answer-field/id #uuid "2ebe645c-97a3-5257-bc32-0836ea3ff9c1" :answer-field/key "selection" :answer-field/type {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045493 :db/ident :answer-field.type/radio} :db/id #edb/ref 17592186404524}] :question/difficulty {:db/id #edb/ref 17592186045485 :db/ident :question.difficulty/easy} :question/id #uuid "200a95d9-6cef-55b2-a6a6-5c194d5765aa" :question/math-academy-id "q-91163" :question/problem "$$\nA=\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\n$$\nB=\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix}\n$$\n\nBy applying elementary row operations of the form ${R}_{i}:={R}_{i}+k{R}_{2},$ the matrix $A$ can be transformed into the matrix $B.$ What are the elementary row operations?" :question/worked-solution "To transform $A$ into $B,$ we need to make the entries above and below ${a}_{23}=-3$ equal to $0.$\n\nTo do this, we can apply the following elementary row operations:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}A & =\\begin{bmatrix}-1 & 1 & 6 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{1}: &={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -3 & -6 & -9\\end{bmatrix} &  & \\,\\begin{aligned}{R}_{3}: &={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}\\end{aligned} \\\\  & ∼\\begin{bmatrix}3 & -9 & 0 \\\\ 2 & -5 & -3 \\\\ -9 & 9 & 0\\end{bmatrix} \\\\  & =B\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the elementary row operations are\n\n$\\,$ ${R}_{1}:={R}_{1}+2{R}_{2}\\,$ and $\\,{R}_{3}:={R}_{3}-3{R}_{2}.$"}
